    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "formula_reference",
      "content": "## Formula\n\n**Potential Energy Formula:**\n\n_Ep = m × ag × Δh_\n\nWhere:\n- **Ep** = potential energy (J, kJ, kWh)\n- **m** = mass of body (kg)\n- **ag** = acceleration of gravity on earth (9.81 m/s²)\n- **Δh** = change in elevation (m)\n\n## Example Calculation\n\nA body of **1000 kg** is elevated **10 m**:\n\n_Ep = (1000 kg) × (9.81 m/s²) × (10 m) = 98,100 J = 98 kJ = 0.027 kWh_"
    }
